### CODEC + TRANSPORT ISOLATION MATRIX
# One subprocess at a time, start to finish: no two cells and no two payloads
# overlap, because a timed region that shares the machine with a neighbour
# measures the neighbour (SPEC.md rule 1). Nothing here talks to PostgreSQL.
mode: full matrix
rows: 1000000
cpu: AMD Ryzen 7 7700 8-Core Processor
mem: 30 GiB
reps: 3 (format cells; the unit reports the median of the reps)
chunk: 1048576 B (1.0 MiB) per transport message
units run: in the dev image
report: /src/bench/results/codec-transport.log
payload dir: /src/bench/internals/codec_transport/build/payloads-haxboi58 (removed on success)
git: 263e514-dirty
# matrix: formats {fpcolumn, arrow-ipc} x transports {shm, uds}; format cells are
# in-process (transport held out), transport cells move the emitted payloads
# (codec held out). Every number is a unit's own JSON field; the runner times
# nothing itself.
# run: fpcolumn: encode + decode in one process (rows=1000000, reps=3)
# run: arrow-ipc: encode + decode in one process (rows=1000000, reps=3)
# run: fpcolumn payload over shm (chunk=1048576 B)
# run: fpcolumn payload over uds (chunk=1048576 B)
# run: arrow-ipc payload over shm (chunk=1048576 B)
# run: arrow-ipc payload over uds (chunk=1048576 B)
# checks: 6 cells; checksums identical among the 2 that reported them; every transport accounted for its whole payload
# checksum: sum_id=500000500000 sum_stock=249500000 sum_price_bits=1539195607485251584 trues=500000 text_hash=12856329016581227397
# note: fpcolumn + shm: no logical checksum; it verified the payload bytes against its own fold reference instead
# note: fpcolumn + uds: no logical checksum; it verified the payload bytes against its own fold reference instead
# note: arrow-ipc + shm: no logical checksum; it verified the payload bytes against its own fold reference instead
# note: arrow-ipc + uds: no logical checksum; it verified the payload bytes against its own fold reference instead
# note: fpcolumn + shm: 48 chunks x 1048576 B is an upper bound; payload_bytes=49527976 is the file and 48 chunks cover it (the final chunk is short)
# note: fpcolumn + uds: 48 chunks x 1048576 B is an upper bound; payload_bytes=49527976 is the file and 48 chunks cover it (the final chunk is short)
# note: arrow-ipc + shm: 46 chunks x 1048576 B is an upper bound; payload_bytes=47903600 is the file and 46 chunks cover it (the final chunk is short)
# note: arrow-ipc + uds: 46 chunks x 1048576 B is an upper bound; payload_bytes=47903600 is the file and 46 chunks cover it (the final chunk is short)

### FORMAT — encode -> bytes -> decode + aggregates, one process, no transport (Experiment 1)
cell            payload    rows/s    GB/s  encode ms  decode ms  copies
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
fpcolumn       47.2 MiB   203.22M   10.06        3.2        1.7       1
arrow-ipc      45.7 MiB   107.19M    5.13        7.4        1.9       6

### TRANSPORT — the same payload bytes, producer -> consumer, codec out of the loop (Experiment 2)
# chunk = 1048576 B (1.0 MiB); CPU is user+system over both sides
cell                  payload  chunks    GB/s   p50 ms   p99 ms   CPU ms  prod ms  cons ms  RSS MiB copies
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fpcolumn + shm       47.2 MiB      48   10.60   0.0036   0.0077      4.8      2.1      2.6     51.8      1
fpcolumn + uds       47.2 MiB      48    5.96    0.036    0.403      8.2      3.5      4.8     50.7      2
arrow-ipc + shm      45.7 MiB      46    9.86   0.0040    0.010      4.9      2.2      2.7     50.4      1
arrow-ipc + uds      45.7 MiB      46    6.23    0.036    0.500      7.6      3.0      4.6     49.2      2

### COPIES — counted copies by stage, as the cells named them
# A 0 at a stage means the bytes were aliased or read in place there; the
# counts are the cells' own (SPEC.md: zero-copy is demonstrated by not copying).
  fpcolumn           copies=1  values->payload=1, payload->decoded-views=0, decoded-views->aggregates=0
  arrow-ipc          copies=6  values->arrow_arrays=1, arrow_arrays->ipc_payload=1, ipc_payload->record_batch=0, aggregate_temporaries=3, ipc_payload->emit_file=1
  fpcolumn + shm     copies=1  file page cache -> producer mapping=0, producer mmap -> shm segment=1, shm segment -> consumer (in place)=0
  fpcolumn + uds     copies=2  file page cache -> producer mapping=0, producer mmap -> kernel socket buffer=1, kernel socket buffer -> consumer buffer=1
  arrow-ipc + shm    copies=1  file page cache -> producer mapping=0, producer mmap -> shm segment=1, shm segment -> consumer (in place)=0
  arrow-ipc + uds    copies=2  file page cache -> producer mapping=0, producer mmap -> kernel socket buffer=1, kernel socket buffer -> consumer buffer=1

